    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=536229428_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Office of the President",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary Albright College seeks an organized, professional, and service-oriented Administrative Assistant to support the President and Executive Vice President while also providing administrative assistance to Human Resources and Advancement. This position manages calendars and meetings, processes financial transactions, supports office operations, assists with Human Resources onboarding, manages incoming mail, and serves as the primary receptionist for the area. The position requires strong organization, discretion, professionalism, and the ability to manage multiple priorities. Essential Responsibilities Provide daily administrative support to the President and Executive Vice President. Manage calendars, appointments, meetings, travel arrangements, meeting logistics, and related scheduling needs. Prepare, proofread, organize, and maintain correspondence, reports, presentations, meeting materials, and electronic and paper files. Track deadlines, follow-up items, special projects, institutional initiatives, and Board-related activities as assigned. Process invoices, bills, purchase requests, reimbursements, and other financial transactions. Complete monthly credit card reconciliations, including collecting receipts, identifying account information, and preparing documentation for approval. Maintain appropriate financial records and work with the Finance Office to resolve payment or documentation questions. Serve as the primary receptionist for the President’s Office, Executive Vice President, Human Resources, and Advancement area, welcoming students, employees, alumni, donors, trustees, applicants, vendors, and other visitors. Answer and route calls and general inquiries to the appropriate person or office. Receive, sort, and distribute incoming mail and deliveries for the President’s Office, Advancement, and Human Resources. Assist Human Resources with onboarding, scheduling, employee communications, document preparation, data entry, recordkeeping, orientations, interviews, and other light administrative duties. Maintain strict confidentiality regarding personnel, financial, donor, student, and institutional matters. Provide general administrative support to Advancement, including mailings, event preparation, meeting coordination, donor and alumni correspondence, and other projects. Maintain office supplies, assist with copying, scanning, outgoing mail, deliveries, and general office operations. Exercise sound judgment in prioritizing requests and determining when matters should be directed to senior leadership or another office. Provide backup administrative support and assist with College events and special projects as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent required; associate or bachelor’s degree preferred. Previous administrative, office, executive support, or related experience preferred. Strong organizational, communication, customer service, and time-management skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, and work with limited supervision. Demonstrated discretion and ability to handle confidential information. Proficiency with Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and standard office technology. Experience with calendar management, financial processing, reimbursements, or Human Resources administration preferred. Previous experience in higher education, Human Resources, Advancement, nonprofit organizations, or executive support is a plus. Professional, dependable, collaborative, and comfortable interacting with individuals at all levels of the College and with members of the public. Albright College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating a welcoming and inclusive community.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=634843918_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary: This full-time position, reporting to the Director of Admission is responsible for a full range of recruitment/travel territory management activities in support of the Admission office. The focus of this position is the recruitment, engagement, nurturing, and development of prospective students. Admission responsibilities include student recruitment, counseling, interviewing and group presentations for undergraduate students; recruitment travel outreach, applicant engagement and cultivation, and application read; and a number of specialty project-oriented tasks assigned by the Director of Admission that could include: project management, technology and social media skills; content writing; and, relational building with on-campus and off-campus groups. Candidate must demonstrate a commitment to enhancing equity and inclusion within the staff and across our culturally diverse campus while celebrating people of all statuses and identities. This commitment must shine through all job functions including but not limited to, recruitment of prospective students, staff training, and implementation of project areas and programs. At Albright, we believe our differences make us stronger and empower us to better understand and respect one another in a just and fair manner. Essential Job Functions: Counsel prospective students and families throughout the admission stages of prospect to matriculation including contact at high schools, college fairs, interviews and on-campus programs. Utilize the mediums of text, email, phone calls, in-person counseling sessions, and virtual meetings to build relationships and manage student population. Assume responsibility for recruitment and outreach in a designated territory establishing and maximizing relationships with school counseling staff and knowledge of regions school systems. Maintain flow of quality prospective students analyzing trends in enrollment and marketing activities. Review and read applications making admission and scholarship decisions and recommendations. Manage the Tuition Exchange employee benefit program with guidance from Human Resources. Oversee content calendar of the Admission Social Media accounts Represent the Admission office in both on and off campus meetings, including academic departments, PACAC; SLATE PA Users Group, high school visits and college fairs, weekend recruitment programs. Provide other necessary assistance in order to meet the department’s enrollment plan and the College’s strategic agenda. Qualifications/Prerequisites: COMMUNICATION: Must have excellent written and oral communication skills. Knowledge of social media platforms and ability to maintain office pages. SKILLS: Dynamic personality with humbleness and sense of humor. Strong attention to detail and proven ability to effectively manage multiple tasks and responsibilities Self-starter with ability to be flexible and appropriately address constituents needs Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion Exemplary interpersonal skills with a focus on student service Ability to work collaboratively with others as a part of a team approach Effectively perform work responsibilities in an unsupervised, in a self-directed manner. Ability to understand and access resources in order to coordinate complex projects and operations Familiarity with the Microsoft Office platform and ease in using new technologies. Maintains confidentiality with respect to files, correspondence, reports and other information. Knowledgeable of or willingness to learn the admission and financial aid process and timelines. Experience with virtual platforms – Zooms, Microsoft Teams, video chatting, etc. EDUCATION: Bachelor’s degree expected LICENSES: Drivers license required. Child clearances required.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620329654_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Bus Driver",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlbright College is seeking applications for a Bus Driver for Athletic Events. Responsibilities for this position include the safe and timely operation of vehicles which transport students, faculty and staff between various points of the College community, other designated locations, and to and from athletic contests. The driver is expected to promote a full participation and inclusive environment. Essential Job Functions: 1.Drives bus to transport students, faculty, and staff to specified local or distant points according to time schedule. 2.Regulates heating, lighting, and ventilating systems for passenger comfort. 3.Complies with local traffic regulations. 4.May inspect bus and check gas, oil, and water before departure. 5.May load or unload baggage for passengers. 6.Maintains the bus in a safe and clean condition. 7.Other duties as assigned by the Program or facilities directors. 8.Professional communication skills with a diverse population required. Qualifications/Prerequisites: 1.COMMUNICATION a. Able to follow verbal and written instructions. 2.SKILLS a. Demonstrated commitment to building an inclusive and equitable Albright community, as described in Albright College’s Inclusivity and Equity Statement. b. Fluency in Spanish preferred. 3.EMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE a. 2+ years’ experience as a driver 4.EDUCATION a. High School Diploma/GED required 5.LICENSES a. Commercial driver’s license with passenger endorsement Review of applications for this position will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should complete an application by clicking “Apply Now”. Cover letter, a minimum of two professional references and any other supporting application materials can be uploaded in one document along with the resume. Optional documents may be submitted can include: proof of education/certification, licenses, and letters of recommendation.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=563844750_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Promise Scholars Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nPosition Summary: The Promise Scholars Student Assistant is responsible for general administrative support of the Promise Scholars/ACT 101 Program and its staff.  The Promise Scholars Student Assistant should be available to help with various large and small projects, be interactive with students, assists with mentoring Promise Scholars, should be reliable and committed to maintaining confidentiality when appropriate, and should have a working knowledge of the Promise Scholars services to Promise Scholars students, as well as possessing a general knowledge of college resources and policies.    Essential Job Functions: The Promise Scholars Student Assistant helps with a variety of administrative tasks, serve as a receptionist which includes ensuring the front desk is staffed to receive all phone calls and visitors when administrative assistant is not available. The Promise Scholars Student Assistant will also participate in Peer Allies mentoring Program by being a mentor to First Year students. Performs the following duties:      Receiving and screening incoming calls with an attention to detail and service excellence, as well as handling correspondence, forms, etc.  Greet students and other visitors, answer questions and ask for assistance when needed Support student functions in other departments across the college Assists with event preparation and projects as needed. Assists with Lending Library/Loaner laptops Manages Promise Scholars social media accounts. Maintains office bulletin boards and signage throughout the hallways and lounge. Assists with Peer Allies Program Assists with Creating Fliers for Promise Scholars events (Canva, or other platforms) Makes copies, scans, and performs campus business errands as assigned. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications/Prerequisites:   1.   COMMUNICATION       We expect that Promise Scholars Student Assistants will have a positive perspective of Albright College.   2.   SKILLS The best candidates to be student office assistants are current undergraduate students who are highly dependable, have excellent communication and organizational skills, and enjoys working with others.   All individuals in the Promise Scholars Student Assistant position should exhibit many of the following: Good interpersonal and communication skills Exercise good judgement and professionalism Ability to handle multiple tasks Receptive to feedback and opportunities to share ideas for improving services Ability to maintain confidentiality Ability to work well with office/professional staff, peers, and faculty Ability to be empathetic to students having difficulties Good overall academic ability   3.   EMPLOYMENT EXPERIENCE Promise Scholars Student Assistants are selected on the basis of academic skill, leadership, character, and the ability to communicate well with others.   4.   EDUCATION Overall GPA of at least a 2.7 Good standing with the college   5.  Promise Scholars Student Assistant does need to be a current Promise Scholar.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=620345498_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Music",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAdjunct Faculty – Music Position: Adjunct Faculty in Music Department: Division of Fashion, Media & Creative Arts Appointment: Part-Time / Adjunct The Department of Music invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty position specializing in Collaborative Piano and Choral Accompanying . We seek an accomplished and collaborative pianist who is passionate about supporting student musicians and contributing to the department’s choral program. Our courses are in-person on our beautiful campus in Reading, Pennsylvania. Instructors must generally be able to be physically present on our campus for two days per week for each course. A typical course will be 3 credit hours and opportunities to teach more than one course per semester may be available. Adjunct instructors receive support including office space and teaching material. The successful candidate will provide piano accompaniment and collaborative support for our vocal ensembles in rehearsal and performance. The position offers an opportunity to work closely with students and faculty in a dynamic collegiate music environment. Responsibilities Accompany choral ensembles for rehearsals, performances, and other departmental events. Collaborate with choral conductors, voice faculty, and other music faculty in preparing students and ensembles. Provide piano accompaniment for voice lessons, studio classes, recitals, auditions, juries, and other student performances as needed. Prepare and perform music appropriate to a variety of choral and vocal repertoire. Attend scheduled rehearsals and performances and provide reliable, professional collaborative support. Work effectively with conductors and faculty to interpret repertoire and meet musical and instructional goals. Support a positive, inclusive, and student-centered learning environment. Participate in departmental activities as assigned. Qualifications Master’s degree in Music, Collaborative Piano, Piano Performance, or a related field preferred; exceptional professional experience may be considered in lieu of the degree. Demonstrated experience as a collaborative pianist and/or choral accompanist. Strong piano skills and the ability to prepare and perform repertoire efficiently. Experience working with choirs, vocalists, conductors, and collegiate or pre-collegiate music students. Strong sight-reading, ensemble, rehearsal, and communication skills. Professionalism, flexibility, dependability, and a demonstrated commitment to student learning. Preferred Qualifications Experience accompanying collegiate or community choirs. Experience collaborating with voice faculty and vocal students. Knowledge of a broad range of choral and vocal repertoire. Experience playing for recitals, juries, auditions, or competitions. Strong ability to adapt to the needs of conductors, ensembles, and individual performers. Application Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae/resumé, and contact information for professional references . Applicants may also be asked to provide recordings or other examples of collaborative piano work. Applications will be reviewed immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The Department of Music is committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive environment for students, faculty, and staff. We encourage applications from candidates who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of our musical community. Start Date: January 2027",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=c4e80d96-7749-44bb-aa20-2c7594475725&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=605996432_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct of Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\n\nLocation: Reading\n\nAlbright College seeks an adjunct instructor in Computer Science for undergraduate courses related to introductory programming, object-oriented programming, cybersecurity, and data science. Our growing programs in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, and Artificial Intelligence layer technical education on Albright's strong liberal arts foundation. Our computer science courses also attract students from across multiple other college majors including Cyber Criminology, Game and Simulation Development, and Business. Our courses are in-person on our beautiful campus in Reading, Pennsylvania. Instructors must generally be able to be physically present on our campus for two days per week for each course. A typical course will be 3 or 4 credit hours and opportunities to teach more than one course per semester may be available. Adjunct instructors receive support including office space and teaching material. Teaching experience is preferred but candidates exclusively with industry experience in software engineering, cybersecurity, or data science will be considered. The successful candidate will have strong knowledge of computer science subject matter, enthusiasm for working with undergraduate students, and a passion for teaching. Evening scheduling may be available to accommodate working professionals.",
